expect login: timeout=90
send root
expect Password:
send godel
expect godel#

comment Session managers (elogind scopes) move user processes out of
comment the supervisor tree. Simulate one properly: a detached
comment setsid process with stdio away from the tty, parked in a
comment top-level cgroup godel does not supervise. The inner shell
comment registers its own pid because busybox setsid forks. cgroupfs
comment seq_files hang when read back while a member lives, so the
comment check goes through ps, not through cgroup.procs.
send mkdir /sys/fs/cgroup/stray && echo cg-ok
expect godel# timeout=10
send setsid sh -c "echo $$ > /sys/fs/cgroup/stray/cgroup.procs; exec sleep 10000" </dev/null >/dev/null 2>&1 &
expect godel# timeout=10
send sleep 2
expect godel# timeout=15
send ps | grep -c "sleep 10000"
expect 1 timeout=10
expect godel# timeout=10

comment Poweroff must sweep the stray before disks go read-only: an
comment unsupervised live process would keep writable mmaps alive and
comment force ext4 journal recovery on the next boot.
send godelctl poweroff
expect final sweep timeout=30
expect stray process(es) killed timeout=30
expect remount-ro ok timeout=30
expect powering off timeout=30
